	"notes": "This is a classic programming-book site: every chapter listed down the left side, the chapter you are reading on the right. On a phone that chapter list disappears completely and a menu button takes its place instead of shrinking to fit. The clever part only shows up in the measurements, not the picture: the paragraph column always stays exactly 750 pixels wide, whether the screen is a laptop or a giant ultrawide monitor, and it centres itself in the space next to the sidebar — a wider screen never gives you a longer line of text, only more quiet space around it. The little blue note box and the previous/next chapter buttons both simply match whatever width that text column already is.",
